{"chunk_id": "fe44eb6d0017", "text": "Sita, Lakshmana, and the charioteer Sumantra reach the sacred Ganges during what Sita believes is a brief pilgrimage to visit sages and distribute gifts. Lakshmana, however, is overwhelmed with grief. After ferrying Sita across the Bhagirathi, he finally reveals the truth: Rama has heard public gossip questioning Sita\u2019s purity despite her earlier trial by fire. Though Lakshmana insists she is blameless, Rama fears public condemnation and has ordered that she be left near the hermitages along the river. Lakshmana begs forgiveness for carrying out the command. The scene marks one of the most tragic turns of the Ramayana\u2014Sita\u2019s abandonment while pregnant and the painful conflict between royal duty, public opinion, and personal loyalty.\nLakshmana tearfully reveals that Rama, fearing public scandal, has ordered Sita abandoned near the hermitages by the Ganges.\nThemes: duty vs compassion, public honor, exile, loyalty to king, tragic separation", "vector": [0.012521681375801563, -0.016127120703458786, 0.007761428598314524, 0.00020824010425712913, -0.02078666351735592, 0.005723717622458935, -0.02558048628270626, 0.0071168807335197926, -0.022008618339896202, -0.03523527458310127, 0.024237679317593575, 0.01964527554810047, 0.007063168566673994, 0.02253231219947338, 0.001576120499521494, -0.010292621329426765, 0.04860963672399521, -0.015536285005509853, 0.028897222131490707, -0.016261400654911995, 0.0013369328808039427, -0.023431994020938873, -0.0069221737794578075, 0.01977955736219883, -0.026923293247818947, -0.004380910191684961, 0.029461201280355453, -0.03064287081360817, 0.019980978220701218, -0.028736084699630737, -0.017563924193382263, -0.017080513760447502, -0.019564708694815636, -0.011467577889561653, -0.028977788984775543, 0.001149779069237411, 0.00043305548024363816, -0.008734963834285736, -0.006707324180752039, -0.011192302219569683, 0.004793823231011629, -0.0014326079981401563, -0.02230403572320938, 0.013508644